Doctor of Science

**Abstract**

The inclusive jet cross section, the dijet cross section, and the dijet longitudinal double spin asymmetry \({\cal A}_{\rm LL}\) in polarized proton-proton collisions at \(\sqrt{s}=200\) GeV are measured with a data sample of \(5.4\mbox{\,pb}^{-1}\) collected with the STAR detector during RHIC Run-6. The inclusive jet cross section is measured as a function of jet transverse momentum \(p_{\rm T}\) in the range of \(13<p_{\rm T}<66\) GeV in the mid-rapidity region \(|\eta|\leq 0.8\). The results are in agreement with NLO pQCD predictions. The dijet cross section and the dijet \({\cal A}_{\rm LL}\) are measured as a function of dijet mass \(M_{\rm jj}\) in the range of \(24<M_{\rm jj}<118\) GeV. The dijet cross section is in agreement with NLO pQCD predictions. The dijet \({\cal A}_{\rm LL}\) is compared with NLO pQCD predictions based on various parametrizations of polarized gluon distributions of the proton. The results are inconsistent with large gluon polarization and expected to lead to a constrain on the polarized gluon distribution.

