### 12.4 The Correction Factors

As discussed in Section 9.4, the correction factors \(\mathcal{C}\) are the products of the two correction factors:

\[\mathcal{C}=\mathcal{C}_{\text{tb}}\cdot\mathcal{C}_{\text{det}}. \tag{12.2}\]

\(\mathcal{C}_{\text{tb}}\), which corrects for the effect of the timebin selections, is common to all final state and is determined in Section 5.7.

